          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "kumārī is the feminine of kumāra, \"boy\", made with the ending -ī (MW). The Atharvaveda already has it as \"young girl\" (CDIAL 3303), and Punjabi kãvārī, \"virgin\", comes from it. India's southern tip, Kanyakumari, is named after the maiden goddess."
            }
          ]
